=head2 SDL_TextInputType

Text input type.

=over

=item SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_TEXT = 0 - The input is text

=item SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_TEXT_NAME = 1 - The input is a person's name

=item SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_TEXT_EMAIL = 2 - The input is an e-mail address

=item SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_TEXT_USERNAME = 3 - The input is a username

=item SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_TEXT_PASSWORD_HIDDEN = 4 - The input is a secure password that is hidden

=item SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_TEXT_PASSWORD_VISIBLE = 5 - The input is a secure password that is visible

=item SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_NUMBER = 6 - The input is a number

=item SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_NUMBER_PASSWORD_HIDDEN = 7 - The input is a secure PIN that is hidden

=item SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_NUMBER_PASSWORD_VISIBLE = 8 - The input is a secure PIN that is visible

=back

=head2 SDL_Capitalization

Auto capitalization type.

=over

=item SDL_CAPITALIZE_NONE = 0 - No auto-capitalization will be done

=item SDL_CAPITALIZE_SENTENCES = 1 - The first letter of sentences will be capitalized

=item SDL_CAPITALIZE_WORDS = 2 - The first letter of words will be capitalized

=item SDL_CAPITALIZE_LETTERS = 3 - All letters will be capitalized

=back



